.TH LOSLES 1 "July 2026" "losles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
losles \- color-managed image viewer with lossless editing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B losles
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B losles
is a lightweight GTK viewer for JPEG and PNG images.
It interprets an embedded image profile and converts the image directly to
the RGB ICC profile selected for the active monitor.
RGB images without a usable embedded profile are assumed to be sRGB;
grayscale images use a D65 gamma-2.2 assumption.
If no monitor profile can be loaded, losles uses an explicit sRGB display
fallback.
.PP
Opening a file also discovers supported images in its parent directory for
previous/next navigation.
Nearby images are decoded and color-converted in the background.
The parent directory is monitored, so externally changed images and the
navigation list are reloaded automatically.
Cached decoded images are checked against the current file state before use.
.SH EDITING AND FILE SAFETY
Editing is immediate and in place.
Lossless JPEG operations rearrange DCT coefficients without decoding and
re-encoding lossy image data.
Supported PNG operations preserve sample values but recompress the PNG image
data.
.PP
Rotation and EXIF-orientation normalization overwrite the original path
without keeping a Trash backup when TurboJPEG reports no warning.
Crop moves the exact original to the system Trash before installing the
cropped replacement.
The
.B Delete
shortcut also moves the current file to Trash.
.PP
Before any edit, losles compares the complete encoded file with the source
that was decoded for display and checks it again before replacement.
If the file changed externally or while the operation was running, the edit
is refused without modifying the file and an error is shown.
.PP
JPEG transforms require a mathematically perfect coefficient operation.
An operation fails rather than discarding incomplete edge blocks.
JPEG crop is available only when EXIF orientation is 1; use the warning-icon
Normalize control first when a non-default orientation is stored.
.PP
Every JPEG edit first stops on TurboJPEG warnings and leaves the source
unchanged if one occurs.
Losles then asks whether to continue.
An approved retry allows warnings without verifying that the result is
complete or undamaged, and moves the exact original to Trash before installing
the replacement.
This applies to rotation, EXIF-orientation normalization, and crop.
.PP
PNG editing is limited to static, non-interlaced, direct-color 8-bit
grayscale, grayscale-alpha, RGB, and RGBA files.
Other supported PNG encodings remain view-only.
.PP
Metadata is retained.
The libjpeg-turbo transform may update recognized EXIF pixel-dimension fields,
but embedded thumbnails and other dimension-dependent metadata are not
generally regenerated after editing and can describe the pre-edit image.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open an image.
.TP
.B Left, Right
Show the previous or next image.
.TP
.B I
Toggle the image and color-profile information overlay.
.TP
.B C
Enter or leave Crop mode.
.TP
.B Enter
Apply the current crop selection.
.TP
.B Escape
Leave Crop mode, or reset a zoomed image to its fitted size.
It does not leave fullscreen.
.TP
.B Alt+Enter
Enter or leave fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B Delete
Move the current image to the system Trash, then show its successor or, when
the deleted image was last, its predecessor.
.SH MOUSE CONTROLS
.TP
.B Back, Forward
Show the previous or next image.
When two adjacent images have the same displayed pixel dimensions, the zoom
level and pan position are retained.
.TP
.B Mouse wheel
Zoom at the pointer.
.TP
.B Primary-button drag
Pan a zoomed image.
.TP
.B Double-click
Enter or leave fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B File drag and drop
Open the first dropped image unless Crop mode or another file operation is
active.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B G_MESSAGES_DEBUG=losles
Enable diagnostic messages about monitor and display-profile selection.
.SH FILES
Packaged installations normally use a prefix of
.IR /usr ;
the default source installation prefix is
.IR /usr/local .
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/applications/io.github.develancer.losles.desktop
Desktop launcher and image MIME associations.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/metainfo/io.github.develancer.losles.metainfo.xml
AppStream software-catalogue metadata.
.TP
.I PREFIX/share/icons/hicolor/512x512/apps/io.github.develancer.losles.png
Application icon.
